  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-7" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Netherlands</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Demand Side Subsidies (DSS) - Rijksdienst voor Ondernemend Nederland (RVO)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Energizing Development (EnDev) is a multi-donor partnership between the governments of the Netherlands, Germany, Norway, and Switzerland. It is co-managed by The Netherlands Enterprise Agency (RVO) and Deutsche Gesellschaft f&#xfc;r Internationale Zusammenarbeit (GIZ) through the German Federal Ministry for Economic Cooperation and Development (BMZ). EnDev focuses on decentralised energy solutions and supports market development for modern energy facilities, especially in rural areas in Sub-Sahara Africa. The Demand Side Subsidies Component (DSS) is a pilot implemented under EnDev. It pilots new demand side subsidy mechanisms in four Sub-Saharan African countries to facilitate access to modern, reliable and affordable energy services &#x2014; encompassing off-grid solar and clean cooking solutions. It targets low-income and displaced populations who are not currently reached by commercial markets. DSS has been extended by one year through a cost-neutral extension until 31-12-2026.</narrative>
  </description>
